"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1724,"**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Isa, narrated to us Salamah ibn al-Fadl, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Muhammad ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrated to me. Also, narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari, narrated to us 'Abd al-A'la, narrated to us Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, from Abu Umamah. Al-Fadl said: from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik. And Muhammad ibn 'Isa said: from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik.

He said: ""I used to lead Abu Ka'b ibn Malik when his sight had failed him. Whenever I took him out to the Friday prayer, and he heard the call to prayer for it, he would supplicate for Abu Umamah As'ad ibn Zurarah. He continued doing this for some time—whenever he heard the Friday call to prayer, he would supplicate for him and seek forgiveness for him. So I said to myself: 'By Allah, this is a burden upon me, why do I not ask him what is the matter with him? Why does he supplicate for Abu Umamah As'ad ibn Zurarah whenever he hears the Friday call to prayer?'

So I took him out on a Friday as I used to do. When he heard the Friday call to prayer, he supplicated for Abu Umamah and sought forgiveness for him. I said to him: 'O my father, why is it that whenever you hear the Friday call to prayer, you supplicate for Abu Umamah?'

He said: 'O my son, he was the first to establish the Friday prayer in Medina at Hazm Banu Bayadah, which is called Naqi' al-Khadamat. I said: 'And how many were you on that day?'

He said: 'Forty men.'"""
